msgid "About CVE-2022-4116"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we are announcing the release of Quarkus 2.14.2.Final and Quarkus 2."
"13.5.Final."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both releases fix https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2022-4116[CVE-"
"2022-4116] which has been rated as severity high."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This fix also hardens CORS handling, including changing 200 OK to 403 "
"FORBIDDEN when a CORS request is rejected because of an invalid origin."
msgstr ""

msgid "It is highly recommended to upgrade to these new versions:"
msgstr ""

msgid "2.14.2.Final contains this fix and several others"
msgstr ""

msgid "2.13.5.Final targets the 2.13 branch and contains this fix only"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Users of the Red Hat Build of Quarkus should update to the https://access."
"redhat.com/articles/6643671[latest 2.7.6.Final-redhat-00012]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"CVE-2022-4116 is a vulnerability in our Dev UI that could lead to remote "
"code execution on the machine running the Dev UI,\n"
"if you go to a carefully crafted webpage while the Dev UI is running."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While it only affects Dev Mode, the impact is still high, as it could lead "
"to an attacker getting local access to your development box."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Joseph Beeton from Constrast Security explains the issue in detail in https:/"
"/www.contrastsecurity.com/security-influencers/localhost-attack-against-"
"quarkus-developers-contrast-security[this blog post]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mitigations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The easiest way to mitigate the issue is to upgrade to either 2.14.2.Final "
"or 2.13.5.Final."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you cannot upgrade right now, a possible workaround is to use a random "
"path for the Quarkus Dev UI by moving all the non application endpoints to a "
"random root:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Dev UI is then available at the following URL: `http://localhost:8080/"
"<your random string>/dev/`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that this also affects other non application endpoints such as the "
"health endpoints (but only in dev mode as we use the `dev` profile)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Credits"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We would like to thank Joseph Beeton from https://www.contrastsecurity.com/"
"[Contrast Security] for reporting responsibly this security issue, and "
"providing both an in depth analysis of the problem and a reproducer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/2.14.2."
"Final[the full changelog of 2.14.2.Final] and https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/releases/tag/2.13.5.Final[the one for 2.13.5.Final] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
